        <p class="text-[18px] leading-[28.8px] font-normal font-sans text-[rgb(34,34,34)] mb-6">
          Recent data reveals a fundamental shift in how people search and find information. Only 40.3% of U.S. Google searchers clicked on an organic result in March 2025, down from 44.2% the prior year, while zero-click searches increased from 24.4% to 27.2% in the same period [Search Engine Land, 2025]. This dramatic transformation means traditional ranking positions matter less than appearing in Google AI Overviews (formerly SGE), Featured Snippets and Answer Boxes, Knowledge Panels and Local Packs, and crucially, LLM Citations across ChatGPT, Claude, and Perplexity.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-[24px] leading-[33.6px] font-bold font-serif text-[rgb(34,34,34)] mb-4">The AI Search Explosion</h3>
        <p class="text-[18px] leading-[28.8px] font-normal font-sans text-[rgb(34,34,34)] mb-6">
          The impact extends far beyond Google. Bain's research finds that about 80% of consumers now rely on "zero-click" results in at least 40% of their searches, reducing organic web traffic by an estimated 15% to 25% [Bain & Company, 2025]. AI Overviews have grown from 6.49% of queries in January 2025 to 13.14% in March 2025 [Semrush, 2025], while ChatGPT traffic surpassed Bing in 2024, marking a fundamental shift in information discovery [Analyzify, 2025]. With the LLM market projected to grow 36% annually through 2030 [Invoca, 2025] and 50% of search engine traffic predicted to shift by 2028 according to Gartner [DesignRush, 2025], businesses must adapt now or risk invisibility.
        </p>

